---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: notes.trim()
---
`required_choice`: use either `--required-choice` or its object options (`--required-choice-label`, `--required-choice-count`). Do not combine the two forms. One form is required.

`optional_choice`: use either `--optional-choice` or its object options (`--optional-choice-label`, `--optional-choice-count`). Do not combine the two forms. Both forms may be omitted.

`settings.outer_choice`: use either `--settings-outer-choice` or its object options (`--settings-outer-choice-choice`, `--settings-outer-choice-choice-label`, `--settings-outer-choice-choice-count`). Do not combine the two forms. One form is required when `settings` is activated.

`settings.outer_choice.choice`: use either `--settings-outer-choice-choice` or its object options (`--settings-outer-choice-choice-label`, `--settings-outer-choice-choice-count`). Do not combine the two forms. One form is required when the object form of `settings.outer_choice` is selected.

`settings.required_group.choice`: use either `--settings-required-group-choice` or its object options (`--settings-required-group-choice-label`, `--settings-required-group-choice-count`). Do not combine the two forms. One form is required when `settings` is activated.

`settings.optional_group.choice`: use either `--settings-optional-group-choice` or its object options (`--settings-optional-group-choice-label`, `--settings-optional-group-choice-count`). Do not combine the two forms. One form is required when `settings.optional_group` is activated.
